---
import Layout from '../../layouts/PhotosSaverLayout.astro'

const title = 'Privacy Policy - Photos Saver'
const description =
  'Privacy Policy for Photos Saver, a Google Photos companion app by Anas Alqoyyum.'
---

<Layout title={title} description={description}>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl">
    <header class="border-b border-stone-200 pb-5 dark:border-zinc-800">
      <h1
        class="text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-stone-950 dark:text-zinc-50"
      >
        Privacy Policy
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-stone-600 dark:text-zinc-400">
        Last updated: August 2, 2026
      </p>
    </header>

    <div
      class="mt-8 space-y-8 text-[15px] leading-7 text-stone-700 dark:text-zinc-300"
    >
      <section class="space-y-3">
        <p>
          This Privacy Policy explains how Photos Saver collects, uses, and
          stores information when you use the Photos Saver browser extension and
          its supporting backend service. Photos Saver is operated by Anas
          Alqoyyum.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2
          class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-stone-950 dark:text-zinc-50"
        >
          Information used by Photos Saver
        </h2>
        <p>
          Photos Saver only requests and processes the information needed to
          provide the upload flow.
        </p>
        <ul
          class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 marker:text-stone-400 dark:marker:text-zinc-600"
        >
          <li>
            Google account identity information provided during sign-in,
            including the stable Google user identifier used to associate your
            authorization with your Photos Saver session.
          </li>
          <li>
            Google OAuth tokens, including an encrypted refresh token stored by
            the backend so the app can request new access tokens when needed.
          </li>
          <li>
            Image upload data that you explicitly send, including the image
            payload, filename, source URL, content type, and optional page URL.
          </li>
          <li>
            Temporary session and auth records needed to complete sign-in and
            maintain an authenticated session.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2
          class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-stone-950 dark:text-zinc-50"
        >
          How information is used
        </h2>
        <ul
          class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 marker:text-stone-400 dark:marker:text-zinc-600"
        >
          <li>Authenticate you with Google.</li>
          <li>Upload images you choose to your Google Photos library.</li>
          <li>
            Maintain session continuity and keep the app working securely.
          </li>
          <li>Diagnose operational or security issues when needed.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          The source URL and optional page URL are added to the description of
          the media item created in your Google Photos library. Photos Saver
          does not read, list, modify, or delete media already in your library.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2
          class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-stone-950 dark:text-zinc-50"
        >
          Storage and retention
        </h2>
        <p>
          Google refresh tokens are encrypted at rest in the backend data store
          and retained until they are replaced or you request deletion. The
          browser extension stores a temporary Photos Saver session token in
          local extension storage.
        </p>
        <p>
          Temporary authorization state expires within 10 minutes, one-time
          exchange codes expire within 5 minutes, and backend sessions expire
          automatically according to the configured session period. Expired
          temporary records are deleted automatically.
        </p>
        <p>
          Photos Saver does not intentionally retain image payloads, filenames,
          source URLs, page URLs, or content types in its backend after an
          upload request finishes. The selected image, filename, and URL-based
          description are sent to Google Photos and remain there according to
          your Google Photos settings until you delete them.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2
          class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-stone-950 dark:text-zinc-50"
        >
          Third-party services
        </h2>
        <p>
          Photos Saver relies on third-party infrastructure to operate,
          including:
        </p>
        <ul
          class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 marker:text-stone-400 dark:marker:text-zinc-600"
        >
          <li>Google APIs and Google Photos</li>
          <li>
            Cloudflare Workers, KV, and D1 for backend hosting and storage
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Those services may process data as required to provide their
          platforms. Their handling of data is governed by their own terms and
          privacy policies.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2
          class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-stone-950 dark:text-zinc-50"
        >
          Data sharing
        </h2>
        <p>
          Photos Saver does not sell personal data or use Google user data for
          advertising, credit decisions, or training generalized artificial
          intelligence or machine-learning models. Data is transferred only to
          Google Photos at your direction and to service providers needed to
          operate Photos Saver, or when required for security or by law.
        </p>
        <p>
          Photos Saver's use and transfer of information received from Google
          APIs adheres to the
          <a
            href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noreferrer noopener"
            class="border-b border-stone-300 pb-0.5 text-stone-950 transition-colors duration-150 hover:border-stone-500 dark:border-zinc-700 dark:text-zinc-100 dark:hover:border-zinc-500"
          >
            Google API Services User Data Policy
          </a>, including the Limited Use requirements.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2
          class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-stone-950 dark:text-zinc-50"
        >
          Managing and deleting your data
        </h2>
        <p>
          You can revoke Photos Saver's access from your
          <a
            href="https://myaccount.google.com/connections"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noreferrer noopener"
            class="border-b border-stone-300 pb-0.5 text-stone-950 transition-colors duration-150 hover:border-stone-500 dark:border-zinc-700 dark:text-zinc-100 dark:hover:border-zinc-500"
          >
            Google Account connections
          </a>. Revocation prevents the stored refresh token from obtaining new
          access tokens but does not itself remove the encrypted record from the
          Photos Saver backend. You can delete uploaded images and their
          descriptions directly in Google Photos.
        </p>
        <p>
          To request deletion of your Google user identifier, encrypted refresh
          token, and active Photos Saver sessions from the Photos Saver backend,
          email
          <a
            href="mailto:doublezero13@gmail.com?subject=Photos%20Saver%20data%20deletion%20request"
            class="border-b border-stone-300 pb-0.5 text-stone-950 transition-colors duration-150 hover:border-stone-500 dark:border-zinc-700 dark:text-zinc-100 dark:hover:border-zinc-500"
          >
            doublezero13@gmail.com
          </a>
          from the Google account you used with Photos Saver. After confirming the
          request, the associated backend records will be deleted. This does not
          delete media from your Google Photos library.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2
          class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-stone-950 dark:text-zinc-50"
        >
          Contact
        </h2>
        <p>
          For privacy questions or requests, email
          <a
            href="mailto:doublezero13@gmail.com?subject=Photos%20Saver%20privacy"
            class="border-b border-stone-300 pb-0.5 text-stone-950 transition-colors duration-150 hover:border-stone-500 dark:border-zinc-700 dark:text-zinc-100 dark:hover:border-zinc-500"
          >
            doublezero13@gmail.com
          </a>.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>
